module gunbc.guarantee_stall.narrowing_arm_not_a_function_of_the_rendering_stall

import gunbc.guarantee_rung { Mitigatable, StructurallyGuaranteed }
import gunbc.guarantee_stall { GuaranteeStall, AwaitsOneGrounding, UncountedNotEnumerable }

// THE DISCRIMINATING FACT IS AN EQUALITY: two positions the checker renders IDENTICALLY took
// OPPOSITE arms. extdeps.github.app:112 and gunbc.auth.secret_rotation:341 were ACCUSED at a
// position rendered 'Node(fn)', while 114 of the 120 DECLINED lines in the same run rendered
// 'Node(fn)' too. No predicate over the shown text can separate arms whose shown text is equal,
// which is why this is an OBSERVABILITY defect and not a reach gap -- a reach gap would be closed
// by widening a predicate.
//
// WHERE THAT MEASUREMENT CAME FROM, stated because it decides how a reader can check it: a
// substitution-aware decline candidate that was built, measured, and WITHDRAWN. It is not in this
// tree. So the equality is NOT re-derivable from the committed corpus, and this row does not claim
// it is. Re-deriving it means rebuilding the candidate. The row is filed anyway because the defect
// it names is a property of the SURVIVING check -- what the narrowing diagnostic renders -- and
// that is unchanged by the candidate's withdrawal.
//
// ONE CITED SITE'S ARM MOVED TWICE, FOR TWO DIFFERENT REASONS, and the second move corrects a
// claim this row made in an earlier revision. Three measurements, each naming its tree:
//   candidate present, before merging main  -> extdeps.github.app:112 ACCUSED
//   candidate absent,  before merging main  -> NOT accused
//   candidate absent,  after merging main   -> ACCUSED again
// The first two differ only in the candidate, so the candidate did perturb an arm at a site it was
// never aimed at. But an earlier revision of this row went on to say that only
// gunbc.auth.secret_rotation:341 is still accused, and that is FALSE for the shipped tree: merging
// main re-accused app:112 for some third reason, without either the candidate or that file changing.
//
// So the site moved for a reason invisible in what the checker showed, TWICE, and the second time
// the invisible reason was somebody else's merge. That is the row's own subject arriving in the
// row's own evidence, and the correction is recorded rather than quietly applied because the false
// sentence was published and a reader may have carried it.
//
// THE MEASURED CONSEQUENCE, which is what makes the class real rather than a story: an attempt to
// predict the arms from source SHAPE -- fold_list cons: positions and Accepted { value: ... }
// positions -- named 17 sites and moved 0 of them. Recognizing a shape in the source is not knowing
// what the checker consumes, and a third group in that census rendered 'Primitive()' and was never
// a generic formal at all, so the census was mixing three mechanisms under one name. The count
// would have concealed all of it: accused fell 42 -> 17 and read as a win while zero intended sites
// moved and the entire drop came from unrelated repairs. Only a site-identity join refused it.
data narrowing_arm_not_a_function_of_the_rendering_stall: GuaranteeStall = GuaranteeStall {
  subject: "the optional-into-required check decides its arm using facts its diagnostic does not render, so positions whose declared type prints identically can take opposite arms and no reader -- author, reviewer, or a later repair pass -- can predict from what the compiler shows them which arm a position will take",
  current: Mitigatable,
  ceiling: StructurallyGuaranteed,
  blocker: AwaitsOneGrounding { grounding: "the narrowing diagnostic renders the FACT THE ARM WAS DECIDED ON -- whether the declared formal at this position was substituted, and by what -- rather than the post-hoc printing of a type whose rendering is equal across both arms" },
  population: UncountedNotEnumerable { reason: "the subject is every POSITION whose rendered declared type hides the fact its arm was decided on, and every reader exposed to one. That set cannot be enumerated from this tree for the same reason the row's own evidence cannot be re-derived from it: the arms were observed only under a decline candidate that was measured and then WITHDRAWN, one of the two positions cited above no longer takes the arm it took then, and the committed corpus produces no declines at all -- so there is no run against this tree that separates a position whose rendering hides the deciding fact from one whose rendering does not. Naming optional_into_required_mismatch and optional_narrowing_diags here would be naming the two MECHANISM CARRIERS, and a carrier cannot answer for the population it exposes: the same two functions serve every position in the corpus, including all the ones that are not affected. The exposure becomes enumerable by exactly the capability the blocker names -- once the diagnostic carries the deciding fact, the affected positions are the ones whose text changes" }
  next_rung_trigger: "the diagnostic CARRIES the deciding fact and a reader CONSUMES it -- sufficient for two positions that render identically today to render differently once the deciding fact is carried, demonstrated by a fixture pair built to render identically and a run showing them distinguishable BY THE DIAGNOSTIC TEXT ALONE. A richer type rendering that leaves such a pair's texts equal does NOT retire this row, because the equality is the defect and a longer string preserving it has changed nothing. Note that the demonstration requires a PURPOSE-BUILT FIXTURE PAIR and not the two historical sites, because those sites arms have already been observed moving under changes aimed at neither of them -- once under the withdrawn candidate and once under an unrelated merge -- so anything derived from their current arm is measuring whatever last moved the tree"
}
